  "$comment": "wagmi (#85): actions (`readContract(config, {...})`, also from `@wagmi/core`) and hooks (`useReadContract({...})`) send JSON-RPC through the transports of the app's config, `createConfig({ transports: { [chain.id]: http(url) } })` (or the `client({ chain })` it is given), the one an action or a hook's `config` option names, else the one the app gives `<WagmiProvider config>` (a config another library builds is not read: no call), else the project's one config. Several transports (one per chain, a `fallback`) leave the host unknown; a config whose transport is a wallet's (`custom`, `unstable_connector`) or a socket gives no call. `usePublicClient()` / `getPublicClient(config)` hand out that config's client, whose methods are viem's. Writes (`writeContract`, `sendTransaction`, `useWriteContract`) go through the connected wallet and are not listed: they are no HTTP request of the app. `rpc` is the method on the wire.",
